      "extract": "If our world, as is widely believed, is quantum, it is in principle representable as a single vector evolving in Hilbert space, and thus, all spatiotemporal notions must be reducible to this description. This suggests a research program that has been variously called ‘Hilbert Space Fundamentalism’ [1], ‘Mad Dog Everettianism’ [2], ‘extreme Occam’s razor’ [3], or simply ‘physics from scratch’ [4]. Essentially, rather",
      "extractCut": true
